ntent: string;\n    80→}\n    81→```\n    82→\n    83→## Streaming Architecture\n    84→\n    85→Messages support three-phase streaming for real-time responsiveness:\n    86→\n    87→```typescript\n    88→// Phase 1: Start\n    89→{ type: \"TEXT_MESSAGE_START\", messageId: \"msg1\", role: \"assistant\" }\n    90→\n    91→// Phase 2: Content chunks\n    92→{ type: \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\", messageId: \"msg1\", delta: \"Hello \" }\n    93→{ type: \"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\", messageId: \"msg1\", delta: \"there!\" }\n    94→\n    95→// Phase 3: End\n    96→{ type: \"TEXT_MESSAGE_END\", messageId: \"msg1\" }\n    97→```\n    98→\n    99→## Tool Integration\n   100→\n   101→Tool calls are embedded in assistant messages, with results returned via tool messages:\n   102→\n   103→```typescript\n   104→// Assistant message with tool call\n   105→{\n   106→  id: \"msg1\",\n   107→  role: \"assistant\",\n   108→  toolCalls: [{\n   109→    id: \"tc1\",\n   110→    name: \"get_weather\",\n   111→    arguments: { location: \"London\" }\n   112→  }]\n   113→}\n   114→\n   115→// Tool result message\n   116→{\n   117→  id: \"msg2\",\n   118→  role: \"tool\",\n   119→  toolCallId: \"tc1\",\n   120→  content: JSON.stringify({ temperature: 18, conditions: \"cloudy\" })\n   121→}\n   122→```\n   123→\n   124→This creates a traceable chain of actions between the agent and tools.\n   125→\n   126→## Synchronization\n   127→\n   128→Two mechanisms handle message sync:\n   129→\n   130→### Messages Snapshot\n   131→\n   132→Complete snapshot for initialization and major state changes:\n   133→\n   134→```typescript\n   135→{\n   136→  type: \"MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT\",\n   137→  messages: [\n   138→    { id: \"1\", role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" },\n   139→    { id: \"2\", role: \"assistant\", content: \"Hi there!\" }\n   140→  ]\n   141→}\n   142→```\n   143→\n   144→### Streaming\n   145→\n   146→Ongoing interactions use the three-phase streaming pattern for real-time updates.\n   147→\n   14